Protecting women's privacy in public spaces 25LSO-0225, 1.0
act.
FISCAL NOTE
The fiscal impact, in the form of expenditure increases, is indeterminable, but
could be significant.
The Department of Administration and Information indicates there is an
indeterminable expenditure increase related to potential legal claims brought
against the State of Wyoming and costs associated with signage and construction for
rooms or buildings that do not meet the requirements of this bill.
The Wyoming Community College Commission indicates that while there is no fiscal
or personnel impact to the Wyoming Community College Committee, there is an
indeterminable expenditure increase for community college districts related to
signage and construction for rooms or buildings that do not meet the requirements
of this bill.
The University of Wyoming indicates the fiscal impact to the University of Wyoming
is indeterminable but may not be significant.
The Supreme Court indicates the fiscal impact is indeterminable due to an unknown
number of cases.
The Governor's Office and the Department of Corrections indicate there is no
significant fiscal or personnel impact to its agency.
